 267:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****     /* The busy flag is released by the decode completion / the failure path
 268:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * below; the queue re-schedules 16ms after the cache write. */
 269:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****     /* Lua: if body and #body > 8 → decodeRawImageData(body, url, cb);
 270:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * the decode completion (or the sync path below) writes the cache and
 271:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * re-schedules the queue after 16ms.
 272:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * NOTE: bodyLen is the BYTE length from the HTTP client — binary image
 273:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * bodies contain NUL bytes, so strlen() must never be used here (the
 274:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****      * pre-P33 build truncated every PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP at its first NUL). */
